**October 19, 2025 - Vehicle Readiness & GPS Tracking Redesign:**

**🔧 Critical Design Change: Separate Readiness from GPS Tracking**

**Problem Identified:**

- Conflated vehicle readiness with GPS tracking (two different concepts)
- Circular dependency: Tracking stops on return → Crew can't get next assignment
- Manual GPS button served no purpose

**Solution Adopted:**

**1. Vehicle Readiness (NEW):**

- Added `vehicle.readiness.isReady` boolean field
- Crew leader manually toggles "Mark Vehicle Ready"
- Required for dispatcher to assign vehicle
- Independent of GPS tracking
- Defaults to FALSE on login (explicit activation)
- Automatically TRUE when "Returned to Station" clicked
- Can mark NOT READY for breaks, maintenance, refueling

**2. GPS Tracking (AUTOMATIC):**

- NO manual control - fully automatic based on vehicle status
- Tracking ON when: assigned, en_route, on_scene, returning
- Tracking OFF when: available
- Continues during "returning" status (tracks journey back)
- Stops when "Returned to Station" clicked

**3. Vehicle Status During Returning:**

- Vehicle status: "returning"
- Vehicle readiness: TRUE (ready for new assignments)
- GPS: Active (tracking return journey)
- Dispatcher sees: "Returning to Station" badge (blue)
- Vehicle: Immediately selectable for new assignments

**4. Crew Location → Vehicle Location Sync:**

- When crew updates GPS location, vehicle location also updated
- One source of truth for dispatcher map
- Eliminates discrepancy between crew and vehicle positions

**5. Station Integration:**

- 20 stations created using current vehicle locations from seeding script
- Vehicles initialized at station coordinates
- Location reset to station when "Returned to Station" clicked
- Station coordinates used for distance calculations when status="available"

**Key Implementation:**

- Backend: `PUT /api/vehicles/:id/readiness` endpoint
- Mobile: Readiness toggle button (no GPS button)
- Mobile: Automatic GPS management in useEffect
- Backend: Crew location update syncs to vehicle
- Dispatcher: Shows readiness badges and GPS active indicators

**Benefits:**

- ✅ Clear separation of concerns (readiness vs tracking)
- ✅ No circular dependencies
- ✅ Crew has explicit control over availability
- ✅ GPS fully automatic - no crew intervention needed
- ✅ Vehicle available immediately after completing assignment
- ✅ Real-time tracking during return journey
- ✅ Accurate distance calculations using real GPS or station coordinates
- ✅ Simplified demo - one phone sufficient, no simulations needed

